    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch09-13--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch09-13: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.14";
    dc:description "The claim is that the simplest ultimate model should build matter from the same structure as space. Simplicity here is a modeling preference, and every current observation is compatible both with that identification and with matter as separate content on a background. Nothing public distinguishes the two.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/none";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: No observable is specified that would differ between a universe in which space and matter are the same structure and one in which matter is additional data on a spatial substrate, once both reproduce current physics.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "'Simplest' and 'same stuff' are ontological preferences, not measured variables.", "A cellular-automaton-like split between space and contents can be made empirically equivalent by pushing the split below current resolution.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.72"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.142"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch09-13--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
